diff --git a/REQUIREMENTS.md b/REQUIREMENTS.md
index 6b28db4..c93097a 100644
--- a/REQUIREMENTS.md
+++ b/REQUIREMENTS.md
@@ -1018,6 +1018,10 @@ access + a validation step server-side.
 | 2026-10-12 | `TransactionIngestor`: the review counter and capture timestamp are now recorded immediately after the insert, and each optional post-insert step (unusual-spend alert, budget warning, price-change alert, widget refresh) runs isolated in `runExtra` | Defect I introduced earlier: the counter and widget refresh ran AFTER three notification detectors with no isolation, so any exception in one of them skipped both for that transaction, and enqueue()'s retry could not recover it (on retry the transaction is already stored and is skipped as a duplicate). Whether this actually fired for anyone is unknown. |
 | 2026-10-12 | Settings gained "Rate on Google Play" (opens the store listing via the app's own package name) and "Share with a friend" (share sheet with the listing link) | Google rations the in-app review pop-up and never shows it on sideloaded builds, so it cannot serve as a user-initiated "Rate this app" button; the store link always works. Share gives people a zero-cost way to recommend the app. |
 | 2026-10-12 | How the above was verified: the pure logic (`SenderShape`, `NotificationLines`, `CaptureDiagnosis`, `ReviewPolicy`, `RelativeTime`) was compiled and run with a real `kotlinc` - 67 checks - and mutation-checked (restoring the old threshold of 10 and the suffix-less sender pattern produced 11 failures). The Android-bound code (listener service, ingestor, settings UI, stores, OEM intents) was only syntax-checked and cross-checked by hand; CI is the first real compile, and none of it has run on a device | Stated plainly so the next reader doesn't mistake "tests pass" for "verified on a Redmi". |
+| 2026-10-20 | Ads: one adaptive (anchored) banner now sits directly above the bottom navigation bar and shows on all five tabs (Home, Transactions, Charts, Budgets, Reminders) for free users once UMP consent is resolved. The two per-screen banners on Transactions were removed (the top one pushed the list down), along with the now-unused `isPro`/`canRequestAds` parameters of `TransactionsScreen` and four unused `BannerAdView` imports. `BannerAdView` keeps one `AdView` alive, collapses to zero height on failure, and retries up to 5 times, a minute apart (it used to give up for the life of the screen). Settings keeps its own banner (the nav bar is hidden there). | Ads only showed on 2 screens because each screen placed its own banner. A shell-level slot loads once instead of on every tab switch. Padding and a surface background separate the ad from the nav icons, because AdMob penalises ads that invite accidental taps - exact policy wording was not checked. **Unverified:** no compile and no device run; the banner returned HTTP 403 / code 3 in earlier tests, so whether the new unit fills is unknown. |
+| 2026-10-20 | Charts tab redesign: month switcher and a Spent / Received / Net card at the top; a donut by category (stable colour per category, percent and amount per row); a new daily-spending bar chart with a dashed daily-average line and the peak day highlighted; the 6-month trend now shows spent AND received side by side. Account balances moved to the bottom of the tab. New `ChartMath` holds the arithmetic (days in month, per-day totals, elapsed days for the average, bar fractions, percent label). | The old trend bars were sized as a fraction of a column that also held the labels, so the tallest bar could squeeze its own month label out of view; bars are now explicit dp heights with labels in their own row. The old category bars were all one colour. `ChartMath` was compiled and run with a real `kotlinc` (26 checks) and mutation-checked (3 mutants, all caught). **Unverified:** the Compose layout itself - no compile, no screenshot. Totals follow the app rules (SENT / RECEIVED only; UNKNOWN counts as neither). |
+| 2026-10-20 | Theme-aware colours across Home, Transactions, Budgets, Reminders, Settings, Charts and Onboarding: new `MutedText` (onSurface at 60%) replaces all hardcoded `Color.Gray`; `Color.White` card surfaces now use `colorScheme.surface`; pastel fills (`#FFF3E0`, `#E8F5E9`, `#FFEBEE`, `#EDE7F6`, `#E3F2FD`) became 12% tints of the semantic colours; the `#E0E0E0`/`#EDEDF2` bar tracks and dividers are faint onSurface tints; `netColorFor` became `@Composable`. Left as is: the white dot on the balance-history line, the "BEST VALUE" label, the amber `#F57C00` and the category palette. | Light, Dark and AMOLED themes are offered, but white cards and pastel fills ignored them. A scripted check (tree-sitter) confirmed no theme read sits in a non-composable function or a Canvas/remember/LaunchedEffect lambda. **Unverified:** no compile and no screenshots; contrast in Dark and AMOLED has not been looked at on a device. |
+| 2026-10-20 | Home and navigation: removed the Charts / Budgets / Reminders chips (same three destinations as the bottom bar), made "Recent activity" rows open the Transactions tab (they had `onClick = {}`), gave Budgets a wallet icon (Charts keeps the bar-chart icon) and raised nav labels from 10sp to 11sp. | The chips duplicated the nav bar and pushed content down; a row that looks tappable and does nothing reads as broken. Rows go to the list rather than a detail sheet because the detail dialog is private to `TransactionsScreen`. **Unverified:** no compile and no device run. |
 
 ---
 
